{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U38", "U43", "R32", "R64"],
      "pins": ["U38.3", "U43.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0193"],
      "observed": "The TPS61040 boost-regulator feedback pin U38.3 and the LM2576HVS-5 feedback pin U43.4 share NET0193, which is also the midpoint of the divider from +12V through R64 (1.8M) to GND through R32 (205k).",
      "expected": "The boost converter's +12V feedback divider should not also drive the fixed-5V buck regulator's feedback pin. U43 feedback should sense its regulated +5V output.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"133\") (name \"NET0193\") ... (node (ref \"R32\") (pin \"2\")) ... (node (ref \"R64\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"U38\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"FB\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U43\") (value \"LM2576HVS-5\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R64 NET0193 +12V 1.8Meg\nR32 0 NET0193 205k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U43 receives feedback from the separate +12V boost divider rather than its own +5V output, so the buck converter may not regulate its output correctly.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["U35", "Q10"],
      "pins": ["U35.1", "U35.6", "U35.5", "Q10.1", "Q10.2", "Q10.3"],
      "nets": ["NET0173", "+5V", "Net-(Q10-G)"],
      "observed": "The LTC4412 VIN pin is on USB VBUS (NET0173), and SENSE is on +5V, but Q10's source is on +5V and its drain is on USB VBUS.",
      "expected": "For the LTC4412 P-channel ideal-diode path, Q10 should be oriented with its source at the USB input and drain at the +5V output, so its body diode permits input-to-output current and blocks reverse current.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"126\") (name \"NET0173\") ... (node (ref \"Q10\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\")) ... (node (ref \"U35\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VIN\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"Q10\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\")) ... (node (ref \"U35\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"SENSE\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "\"USB power-path controller intended to OR/protect a USB power input\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The reversed MOSFET body-diode orientation can provide a path for reverse current from the +5V rail back into USB VBUS, defeating the stated reverse-current protection.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the +12V boost feedback node is shared with the fixed-5V buck feedback pin, and the LTC4412-controlled P-channel MOSFET is oriented opposite to the expected ideal-diode direction. Both can compromise power regulation or reverse-current protection."
}

